<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 20 December, from 944 to 2001.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">944 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,082 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Romanos I Lekapenos is deposed by his sons</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-i-lekapenos">Romanos I Lekapenos</a>, regent and senior co-ruler for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-vii">Constantine VII</a> since 920, was arrested by two of his sons and forced to abdicate. He lived out his life as a monk.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-i-lekapenos">Romanos I Lekapenos</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1046">1046 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">980 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Synod of Sutri opens to settle rival claims to the papacy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The council called by Henry III, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, opened at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutri">Sutri</a>, at the edge of the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, to deal with rival claimants to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>. Henry deposed the rival popes and went on to install reforming German popes.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Henry III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1248">1248 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">778 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongol envoys meet Louis IX in Cyprus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a>, bound for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seventh-crusade">Seventh Crusade</a>, received two Mongol envoys bearing a letter from Eljigidei, the Mongol commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. They proposed that Louis land in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> while Eljigidei attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-mongol-alliance">Franco-Mongol alliance</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seventh-crusade">Seventh Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1606">1606 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">420 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Virginia Company ships sail for America</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Susan Constant, Godspeed and Discovery left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> with about 105 colonists. In May 1607 they founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a>, the first permanent English settlement in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1803">1803 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">223 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The United States takes possession of Louisiana</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a ceremony in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> formally handed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> Territory to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. The purchase roughly doubled the country's size and gave it control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1860">1860 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">166 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">South Carolina secedes from the Union</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A convention in Charleston voted unanimously to leave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> after Lincoln's election. Six more states followed before his inauguration, forming the Confederacy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The United States invades Panama</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">US forces launched <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-invasion-of-panama">Operation Just Cause</a> to remove Panama's military ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-noriega">Manuel Noriega</a>, who was wanted in the US on drug trafficking charges. Noriega surrendered on 3 January 1990.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/argentina" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/argentina.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2001">2001 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">25 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Argentina's president resigns amid riots</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-de-la-rua">Fernando de la Rúa</a> resigned and fled the Casa Rosada by helicopter as protests over economic collapse left dozens dead. Days later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> declared the largest sovereign default to that date.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 20 December <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-iii-of-sweden"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-iii-of-sweden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John III of Sweden</span><span class="tp">1537–1592</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-menzies"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-menzies.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert Menzies</span><span class="tp">1894–1978</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 20 December <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-iii-of-asturias"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfonso-iii-of-asturias.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfonso III of Asturias</span><span class="tp">c. 848–910</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/stefan-dusan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Stefan Dušan</span><span class="tp">c. 1308–1355</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/erich-ludendorff"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/erich-ludendorff.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Erich Ludendorff</span><span class="tp">1865–1937</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/luis-carrero-blanco"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/luis-carrero-blanco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Luis Carrero Blanco</span><span class="tp">1904–1973</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leopold-sedar-senghor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopold-sedar-senghor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Léopold Sédar Senghor</span><span class="tp">1906–2001</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
